<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">O'Donovan family</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The O'Donovans, in Irish Ó Donnabháin, are an Irish family descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donnuban-mac-cathail">Donnubán mac Cathail</a>, a 10th-century king of the Uí Fidgenti in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-limerick">County Limerick</a>. Displaced by Anglo-Norman settlers around the early 13th century, they moved south into Carbery in west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cork">Cork</a>. There they held lordships around Castle Donovan and near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skibbereen">Skibbereen</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-maccarthy">MacCarthy</a> princes until the confiscations of the 17th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/odonovan-family.jpg" alt="O'Donovan family" width="320" height="354" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: self-created · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:O%27Donovan.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
